<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26f0df0e40ca06fa598fa5a76da0ac9ea2669564949f275b54dd4750b8cfccd4</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b54d53d15fc08d17cc8f116bd98e1308d6303b61afe6608295476fc5d1019fa8</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Tinubu Must Go!': Nigeria's northern protests test limits of political dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67de2340351693439c60ac10c604d7a9bb7bfdd5dba0c0bd981fbaff399bf7f6</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785--b9a2ff0fa9c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of several men wearing anti-government T-shirts and the disruption of a political meeting have renewed debate over free expression and protest rights in Nigeria.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Cult leader guilty of murdering 190 children, 1 adult</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfa897b7dde0c1e786c3dddb38744f3d2835a2eed7e3b641d1818bfbf3a6a32f</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279--f2f58ea97f8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Preacher Paul Mackenzie was accused of encouraging his followers to starve themselves to death. He ran a Christian doomsday cult called the Good News International Church that claimed the end of the world was imminent.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The Bundestag has debated the genocide Germany carried out in Namibia a century ago. But will it spur progress on addressing colonial crimes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c477e34308c700faf0daf5d419a9d9bf68c7d190824ad5c55afdacb0d9efc41c</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur/a-79682388--50aa326f1793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur-progress-on-addressing-colonial-crimes/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
